{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4452","id":4281746756,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLKB0uM7_NkVE","html_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4452","diff_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4452.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/pull/4452.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/issues/4452","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4452/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/4452/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/issues/4452/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/statuses/22a9e6a3cfc7140b8d606f70c40156e16798d96c","number":4452,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(rollout): align sync and rtc action/state ordering","user":{"login":"Maximellerbach","id":38923282,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTIzMjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38923282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach","html_url":"https://github.com/Maximellerbach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maximellerbach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Stacked on #4057 (base `feat/sync-relative-actions`), so the diff here is just this fix. Retargets to `main` once #4057 lands.\n\n## The bug\n\n`build_dataset_frame` orders `observation.state` by `dataset_features[OBS_STATE][\"names\"]`; `send_next_action` labels the action tensor **positionally** with `ordered_action_keys`. Those two orders must agree, and nothing checked it.\n\n`SyncInferenceEngine.get_action` ended with a `make_robot_action` + reindex round trip that predates #4416 and was *compensating* for an unaligned state. #4416 aligned the state, turning that compensation into a net permutation:\n\n| | state layout | `get_action` | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sync (before) | checkpoint order | remaps via `dataset_features[ACTION][\"names\"]` | ❌ permutes |\n| RTC | checkpoint order | returns raw | ✅ correct |\n\nSo for any checkpoint whose `action_feature_names` order differs from the robot's joint enumeration, sync silently commanded every joint with another joint's value while RTC drove the same checkpoint correctly. RTC was right; sync was the odd one out.\n\nThis matters more with #4057: once relative actions run on sync, `AbsoluteActionsProcessorStep` adds the cached state *positionally*, so the permutation also anchors each joint on another joint's measurement. On mirrored bimanual arms the target moves *away* from the measured position as the joint tracks it, compounding every tick into a runaway rather than a fixed offset. Seen on a `bi_openarm_follower` (`left_*` then `right_*`) running a `right_*`-first checkpoint — a pure rotation by 8, so every joint pairs with its opposite-arm twin.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`sync.py`** — `get_action` returns the policy's own dimension order, matching `RTCInferenceEngine`. This is the fix.\n- **`context.py`** — `_align_action_feature_order`, the action-side counterpart of `_align_state_feature_order`, so `dataset_features[ACTION][\"names\"]` stays consistent with the aligned state and recorded episodes are labelled with the order they were rolled out in. No-ops unless the names are the same set in a different order.\n- **`context.py`** — `_assert_state_matches_action_order` rejects a state/action permutation at context-build time rather than letting it reach the motors. Only genuine permutations fail; robots whose state legitimately differs from the action set (extra `.vel` channels, an uncommanded base) pass.\n- **`rtc.py`** — RTC builds observations from `dataset_features` instead of the raw-hardware `hw_features`. With the default identity `robot_observation_processor` the two are byte-identical today, so this is not a behaviour change — but `build_rollout_context` accepts an injected observation processor, and the first non-identity one would desync RTC's state vector from sync's. It also puts RTC behind the new assertion, which only validates `dataset_features`. The now-dead `hw_features` plumbing is dropped from the factory.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_rollout_action_ordering.py` drives both real engines, the real relative/absolute step pair and the real `send_next_action` against a bimanual stub whose hardware order is the reverse of the checkpoint's. Measurements and per-dimension offsets sit on separate decimal scales, so each commanded value decomposes back into exactly one `(anchor joint, policy dimension)` pair — the tests name *which* joint fed *which* command. Parameterized over the historical wiring variants so the broken ones are reproduced, not merely absent; a happy-path-only test is what let this land. Confirmed the harness fails if the fix is reverted.\n\nTwo behaviours pinned along the way: the grippers carry no anchor and cannot diverge, but the permutation still swaps the two of them with each other (part of why a swapped rollout still opens and closes plausibly); and sync/RTC produce the same commanded dict.\n\n```\npytest tests/test_rollout_action_ordering.py tests/test_rollout.py \\\n       tests/test_interactive_rollout.py tests/policies/rtc \\\n       tests/policies/test_relative_actions.py tests/processor\n# 857 passed, 14 skipped\n```\n\nAlso confirmed on hardware: a `bi_openarm_follower` rollout of a right-arm-first checkpoint drives correctly.\n\n## Supersedes\n\nReplaces #4122, which proposed the opposite fix (making RTC re-order the way sync did) — the asymmetry runs the other way. #4122's three unrelated RTC chunking fixes (hold-padding the RTC prefix, clamping the queue-splice discard, excluding cold starts from the latency tracker) are not included here and are tracked for a follow-up.\n","labels":[{"id":6829388968,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLKB0uM8AAAABlxA0qA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/huggingface/lerobot/labels/tests","name":"tests","description":"Problems with test coverage, failures, or improvements to testing","color":"8dc149","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-14T17:02:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T09:55:11Z","closed_at":"2026-09-22T09:55:09Z","merged_at":"2026-09-22T09:55:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"0120909ed1e1df860217fefa78755015b0315744","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"huggingface:fix/rollout-sync-action-permutation","ref":"fix/rollout-sync-action-permutation","repo":{"id":748713144,"node_id":"R_kgDOLKB0uA","name":"lerobot","full_name":"huggingface/lerobot","owner":{"login":"huggingface","id":25720743,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI1NzIwNzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25720743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/huggingface","html_url":"https://github.com/huggingface","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huggingface/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huggingface/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huggingface/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huggingface/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"http